description:
pkix-path-builder/src/lib.rs:375 (build_path doc):

  // Limitations
  Cycle detection is based on `SubjectPublicKeyInfo` DER identity rather than
  subject DN.

But the actual code at lines 268-273 deliberately does NOT compare full SPKI DER:

  let candidate_spki = &candidate.tbs_certificate.subject_public_key_info;
  let already_in_path = path.iter().any(|in_path| {
      let s = &in_path.tbs_certificate.subject_public_key_info;
      s.algorithm.oid == candidate_spki.algorithm.oid
          && s.subject_public_key == candidate_spki.subject_public_key
  });

The comment block at lines 259-267 explains why DER-equality is intentionally NOT used (RSA NULL vs absent parameters issue). That rationale is correct. But the high-level docstring at line 375 contradicts it by saying 'DER identity'.

Fix: in the public docstring, replace 'DER identity' with 'algorithm OID + raw key bits' (or copy the rationale from lines 259-267 into a 'Cycle detection' bullet).

Pass-1 attribution: not flagged. The internal comment is correct; the public-facing doc was not updated when the SPKI comparison was hardened.
